<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Vane</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1680–<a href="/years/1721">1721</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Vane was an English pirate who operated from Nassau in the Bahamas between 1716 and 1719. He refused the royal pardon brought by Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodes-rogers">Woodes Rogers</a> in 1718, escaped from Nassau harbour by sending a fireship against Rogers's ships, and continued raiding. His crew deposed him in favour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calico-jack">Calico Jack</a> later that year; shipwrecked and captured, he was hanged at Port Royal, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>, in 1721.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-vane.jpg" alt="Charles Vane" width="320" height="475" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Early_18th_century_engraving_of_Charles_Vane.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
